      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;padding:12px 14px;background:#2b3137;color:#e9edf0;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #4a535d\"><h3 style=\"font-size:15px;margin:4px 0 10px 0;color:#ffffff\">Export for MTAT &mdash; size this cluster on Operations' peaks</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">The two tables above are MTAT's own import files, column for column.</b> MTAT (Broadcom's\nMemory Tiering Assessment Tool) sizes new hosts and prices DRAM against NVMe, but from vCenter it only\nsees 2-hour averages over 30 days. These files carry Operations' 5-minute peaks instead.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">Export.</b> Click a cluster, then use each table's CSV export: the hosts table is MTAT's\n<i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">Hosts CSV</i>, the VMs table its <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">VMs CSV</i>. Both cover the last 30 days. Do not re-save them in\nExcel; a re-save can reformat the numbers.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">Import.</b> In MTAT, connect to vCenter (it needs that even to import), pick the\n<i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">same</i> cluster, then <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">Import Data Instead &rarr; MTAT Export (Hosts + VMs CSV)</b>, attach both\nfiles and label the range, for example <code style=\"font-family:monospace;background:#363d45;color:#8fd3ff;padding:1px 3px;border-radius:3px\">Ops 30d peak</code>. A yellow \"imported with notes\"\nmessage is normal.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">Check the result.</b> <code style=\"font-family:monospace;background:#363d45;color:#8fd3ff;padding:1px 3px;border-radius:3px\">Active_GB</code> is each host's own 30-day peak, and MTAT\nadds them up, so its total can sit slightly above the cluster's <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffffff\">Active peak GB</b> when hosts\npeak at different times &mdash; the safe direction, more DRAM rather than less.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#ffd79a\">Never import a file with a \"-\" in a number column</b> &mdash; MTAT reads it as zero. MTAT will\nshow Tiering <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">Unknown</i> and Pinned <i style=\"font-style:italic;color:#e9edf0\">N/A</i>; read pinned memory from the Clusters dashboard.</p></div>",
